# Code Review Checklist

Before completing any task, verify:

## Client Checklist

- [ ] Using `@/` alias for src/ imports
- [ ] Import order is correct (React → libraries → @/ → assets)
- [ ] Using design tokens instead of hardcoded values
- [ ] All props have TypeScript types
- [ ] Using `const` and template literals
- [ ] Components use `useMemo`/`useCallback` where appropriate
- [ ] StyleSheet defined at bottom

## Server Checklist

- [ ] Type hints on all functions
- [ ] Using async/await for DB operations
- [ ] Following Router → Service → Repository pattern
- [ ] Using `@dependency` decorator
- [ ] Proper HTTPException with status codes
- [ ] Using `*,` for keyword-only arguments
- [ ] Eager loading relationships to prevent N+1
- [ ] Import order is correct

## Both Checklist

- [ ] No TODOs or placeholders
- [ ] No hardcoded values that should be configurable
- [ ] No unused imports or variables
- [ ] Error handling is complete
- [ ] Code is readable and self-documenting
